{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'ls work/raft | head -40 && cat update.json | head -80'","aggregated_output":"CHANGELOG.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\napi.go\nassurance_cv_test.go\nassurance_follower_test.go.off\nassurance_fs_test.go\nassurance_generated_test.go.off\nassurance_jitter_test.go\nassurance_pg_test.go\nassurance_phantom_test.go\nassurance_phantom_test.go.keep\nassurance_pp_test.go\nassurance_rb_test.go\nassurance_rc_test.go\nassurance_sr_test.go\nassurance_startup_test.go.off\nassurance_sw_test.go\nassurance_term_test.go.off\nassurance_transfer_test.go.off\nassurance_verify_test.go.off\nassurance_vx_test.go\nassurance_xg_test.go\nbench\nbench_test.go\ncommands.go\ncommitment.go\ncommitment_test.go\nconfig.go\nconfiguration.go\nconfiguration_test.go\ndiscard_snapshot.go\ndiscard_snapshot_test.go\ndocs\nfile_snapshot.go\nfile_snapshot_test.go\nfsm.go\nfuture.go\n{\n  \"rationale\": \"Interpret receipt f87365ea88ba4a48a610ba8f380419b0, which replaces the synthetic delay with a real file write plus fsync on every current-term update. 89 of 200 attempts inverted with a mean write of about 2 ms and a maximum of 16.2 ms, so the exposure is demonstrated under genuine filesystem latency rather than an injected sleep, and the measured mean falls in the range where the earlier sweep showed the rate saturated. The account keeps its conclusion and defect claim, extends the rationale with the receipt, and replaces the counterevidence entry that said the delay was only a sleep before an in-memory write.\",\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"830b0f3ff5a14266b056ad4a6d0c877b-knowledge-0\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"The Transport interface documents SetHeartbeatHandler as a fast-path that avoids head-of-line blocking and tells transports that do not support it to push heartbeats onto the Consumer channel; NetworkTransport stores the callback and, for a request shaped like a heartbeat, calls it directly on the connection-handler goroutine, while InmemTransport ignores the call entirely. NewRaft registers r.processHeartbeat, which forwards the request to appendEntries.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Transport implementing the heartbeat fast-path (NetworkTransport); NewRaft has completed and registered the handler.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"contract_heartbeat_handler\",\n        \"api_set_heartbeat_handler\",\n        \"net_heartbeat_dispatch\",\n        \"net_heartbeat_classify\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {\n        \"cabc782e68fb4c98a4f82a9d4e62e07b\": [\n          0,\n          2\n        ],\n        \"14a6432138534293b361a796cd32bda8\": [\n          0,\n          2\n        ],\n        \"b89fc1d89b434e8c84a2219073e9a01c\": [\n          0,\n          2\n        ],\n        \"0ca5ad7d5e8140febbfcf1311e199a4c\": [\n          0,\n          2\n        ],\n        \"1bec110248d14e9e80aac0f8b8129f1c\": [\n          0,\n          2,\n          4,\n          6,\n          8\n        ],\n        \"f87365ea88ba4a48a610ba8f380419b0\": [\n          0\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"830b0f3ff5a14266b056ad4a6d0c877b-knowledge-1\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"appendEntries raises the receiving term by first testing a.Term against r.getCurrentTerm() and later calling setCurrentTerm(a.Term), which writes the stable store and then the atomic term without comparing against the value it read, so the decision and the write are not a single atomic compare-and-set; the same function later deletes a conflicting log suffix from the first index whose term differs and applies the replacement history.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Any appendEntries invocation, including one delivered concurrently through the heartbeat fast-path; the heartbeat case has PrevLogEntry 0, no entries and LeaderCommitIndex 0.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"raft_append_term_handling\",\n        \"raft_set_current_term\",\n        \"raft_conflict_truncation\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {\n        \"cabc782e68fb4c98a4f82a9d4e62e07b\": [\n          1,\n          3\n        ],\n        \"14a6432138534293b361a796cd32bda8\": [\n          1,\n          3\n        ],\n        \"b89fc1d89b434e8c84a2219073e9a01c\": [\n          1,\n          3\n        ],\n        \"0ca5ad7d5e8140febbfcf1311e199a4c\": [\n          1,\n          3\n        ],\n        \"1bec110248d14e9e80aac0f8b8129f1c\": [\n          1,\n          3,\n          5,\n          7,\n          9\n        ],\n        \"f87365ea88ba4a48a610ba8f380419b0\": [\n          1\n        ]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
