{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd .. && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='submissions/1255b78953904846987cdc19826340c8/raw.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nprint(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k\"'!='\"'experiment'},indent=1)[:1500])\ne=d.get('experiment')\nprint(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in e.items() if k not in ('files',)},indent=1)[:4000])\nprint('FILES', list(e.get('files',{})))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"rationale\": \"Record the sourced startup-replay premise discovered while reading the recovery path, and execute a bounded four-case probe (two boundary controls, two triggers, two of them built from a real single-node cluster prefix) to test whether NewRaft() completes a legal committed-log replay.\",\n \"sources\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"cfg_restore_option\",\n   \"file\": \"config.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 243,\n   \"end_line\": 254,\n   \"kind\": \"document_statement\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"cfg_defaults\",\n   \"file\": \"config.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 329,\n   \"end_line\": 341,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"api_fsm_channel\",\n   \"file\": \"api.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 556,\n   \"end_line\": 562,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"api_restore_call\",\n   \"file\": \"api.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 600,\n   \"end_line\": 610,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"api_start_goroutines\",\n   \"file\": \"api.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 630,\n   \"end_line\": 640,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"api_restore_body\",\n   \"file\": \"api.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 723,\n   \"end_line\": 755,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"api_shutdown\",\n   \"file\": \"api.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 1060,\n   \"end_line\": 1072,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"raft_process_logs\",\n   \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 1296,\n   \"end_line\": 1314,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"raft_batch_flush\",\n   \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 1336,\n   \"end_line\": 1362,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observ\n{\n \"investigation_id\": \"@q_startup_replay\",\n \"harness_path\": \"exp_restore_committed_logs_test.go\",\n \"execution_package\": \".\",\n \"test_names\": [\n  \"TestAssuranceRestoreCommittedLogsStartupReplay\"\n ],\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"cfg_restore_option\",\n  \"cfg_defaults\",\n  \"api_fsm_channel\",\n  \"api_restore_call\",\n  \"api_start_goroutines\",\n  \"api_restore_body\",\n  \"api_shutdown\",\n  \"raft_process_logs\",\n  \"raft_batch_flush\",\n  \"fsm_consumer\",\n  \"store_commit_tracking\"\n ],\n \"scope\": {\n  \"description\": \"Four restart attempts with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled: a commit-tracking store seeded with 8192 committed command entries (exactly 128 batches), the same seeded store with 8193 entries (129 batches), and two restarts of the same-address retained state produced by a real single-node cluster that committed 8300 commands through the normal leader/commit/apply path, one after an explicit Snapshot() and one without a snapshot.\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"The FSM batch channel capacity and MaxAppendEntries are constants of the captured code; the harness records both in every case event.\",\n   \"Each case builds its own stores and transport, so cases do not share state; the real-prefix cases reuse exactly the stores written by the producing raft.\",\n   \"NewRaft is invoked on its own goroutine and observed for a bounded window; a case that never returns is reported as returned=false rather than as a harness failure.\",\n   \"fsm_applied_sampled is a single observation at the end of the window, not a completion marker.\"\n  ],\n  \"excluded\": [\n   \"No assertions about commit safety, voting or membership; this probe addresses startup progress only.\",\n   \"Snapshots older than the staged commit index by fewer than 8193 entries are not varied; the with-snapshot control removes the replay entirely.\"\n  ],\n  \"parameters\": {\n   \"control_128_batches\": {\n    \"entries\": 8192,\n    \"replay_batches\": 128\n   },\n   \"trigger_129_batches\": {\n    \"entries\": 8193,\n    \"replay_batches\": 129\n   },\n   \"control_real_prefix_with_snapshot\": {\n    \"commands\": 8300,\n    \"expected_replay_batches\": 0\n   },\n   \"trigger_real_prefix_no_snapshot\": {\n    \"commands\": 8300,\n    \"expected_replay_batches\": 130\n   },\n   \"timeout_ms\": {\n    \"controls\": 20000,\n    \"triggers\": 5000\n   }\n  }\n },\n \"prefix\": \"Per case the harness creates an InmemCommitTrackingStore (and InmemSnapshotStore, InmemTransport, assuranceFSM) and emits startup_case_<case> with the staged commit index, last log index, snapshot index and derived replay batch count. Seeded cases store LogCommand entries 1..N and stage commit index N. Real-prefix cases call BootstrapCluster for a single voter, start the producing raft with RestoreCommittedLogs=true, wait for leadership, apply 8300 commands through Apply futures on the leader, optionally call Snapshot(), then Shutdown(). The restart then calls NewRaft with a fresh Config (RestoreCommittedLogs=true), a fresh FSM and a fresh transport on the retained stores, bounded by the case timeout; startup_result_<case> records returned, elapsed_ms, error, sampled FSM apply count and the number of newly blocked processLogs/restoreFromCommittedLogs goroutines relative to a pre-case stack sample.\",\n \"responsibility\": \"The library, not the caller, owns the size and lifetime of its FSM dispatch channel: it chooses the batch size, creates fsmMutateCh, and decides the order in which NewRaft starts the FSM consumer. The documented RestoreCommittedLogs option promises to replay all known-committed logs on disk before completing NewRaft, so it must complete for a legal (store, commit index) state rather than block the caller that cannot yet shut it down.\",\n \"prerequisites\": [\n  {\n   \"alias\": \"admit_control_128\",\n   \"event\": \"startup_case_control_128_batches\",\n   \"conditions\": [\n    {\n     \"field\": \"restore_committed_logs\",\n     \"value\": true\n    },\n    {\n     \"field\": \"case\",\n     \"value\": \"control_128_batches\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"alias\": \"admit_control_snapshot\",\n   \"event\": \"startup_case_control_real_prefix\nFILES []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
